<title>USA: Centocor sees profit in Q4 1996.</title>
<headline>Centocor sees profit in Q4 1996.</headline>
<dateline>SAN FRANCISCO 1997-01-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Centocor President and Chief Executive Officer David Holveck expects the company to report its first quarterly profit in the fourth quarter of 1996 and expects a $0.20 per share loss for the full year.</p>
<p>In fiscal 1995, the company lost $0.98 a share.</p>
<p>&quot;The turnaround is over,&quot; Holveck said at the Hambrecht &amp; Quist health care conference here.</p>
<p>He said a main factor in the quarterly profit would be a sharp rise in its sales of ReoPro, a drug that helps prevent blood clots in angioplasty patients.</p>
</text>
